Let $e\in\mathcal T_m$ be idempotent and let $z\in e\mathcal T_me$. For a positive recurrent class $C\in\mathcal C_e$ and any $p\in C$, set $$A_C=\{u:u(F_eK_e)p\},\qquad
 B_C=\{v:p(K_eF_e)v\}.$$ The rectangle $A_C\times B_C$ is independent of $p$ and is contained in $F_e$. These rectangles cover $F_e$. If $C\notin\mathcal M_e(z)$, its rectangle is contained in $F_z$. The reflected assertions hold for negative classes and $B_e$. In particular, $$\label{diag:detect}
 \mathcal M_e(z)=\varnothing\quad\Longrightarrow\quad e\sqsubseteq z.$$
